<article class="env-lemma" id="02RC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02RC">Lemma <span data-tag="02RC">42.14.2</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subscheme, and denote $i : Y = X \setminus U \to X$ as a reduced closed subscheme of $X$. For every $k \in \mathbf{Z}$ the sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z_ k(Y) \ar[r]^{i_*} &  Z_ k(X) \ar[r]^{j^*} &  Z_ k(U) \ar[r] &  0 }  \]
</div>
  <p> is an exact complex of abelian groups. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      First assume $X$ is quasi-compact. Then $Z_ k(X)$ is a free $\mathbf{Z}$-module with basis given by the elements $[Z]$ where $Z \subset X$ is integral closed of $\delta $-dimension $k$. Such a basis element maps either to the basis element $[Z \cap U]$ or to zero if $Z \subset Y$. Hence the lemma is clear in this case. The general case is similar and the proof is omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>